n the CLI-level leaf.archive handler, so every ingress path folds on archive.","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","necessity","project.engine-layer-enforcement","project.portability"],"criteria":["project.engine-layer-enforcement"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.9,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'make the fold part of the archive operation itself: rebar archive performs the ticket's final fold inline right before writing the ARCHIVED event'","'leaf.archive (src/rebar/_commands/leaf.py) writes only the ARCHIVED event + .archived marker'","Ingress paths that reach archive: CLI archive command, MCP tool handler, library facade — plan does not state the fold sits in a shared *_core/seam function all three call."],"finding":"Change 1 places the terminal fold inline in `leaf.archive` (src/rebar/_commands/leaf.py). Archive is reachable via three ingress paths (CLI, MCP tool handler, library facade); if the fold is added to the CLI command surface rather than the shared archive write seam, MCP/library archive callers would write ARCHIVED + marker WITHOUT the inline fold, and — once change 2 scopes the default sweep to active-only — their archived tickets carry permanently-stranded unfolded events that no default walk ever reaches.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fc286c73fae9624f0","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 1 / Scope: 'src/rebar/_commands/leaf.py — archive performs the ticket's terminal fold inline before the ARCHIVED event.'","norm_id":"n62ce9479ba387f36","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:cited-reference-inaccurate","recalled":false,"scenarios":["MCP tool call to archive a ticket: if the fold is CLI-local, the MCP path writes ARCHIVED without folding, and the default active-only sweep never revisits it — the tail events are stranded until someone runs --include-archived.","Library facade archive (rebar.archive-equivalent): same bypass — the invariant 'archived ticket is fully folded' holds only for the CLI path."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Locate the shared archive_core (or equivalent seam) that MCP and the library facade also call, and perform the terminal fold there right before the ARCHIVED append_event, leaving leaf.py only as a thin CLI caller.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2222,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"no","cited_reference_accurate":"no","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Clarify in Approach step 2 that only the per-ticket checks that produce per-ticket findings (snapshot consistency, forward-compat) become active-only, while the store-wide authorship-tally checks (JSON-validity, create-events) must still walk every ticket and use `include_archived` to scope REPORTING only — so the tally is not broken and the performance expectation is accurate.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.7413,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan Context: 'the fsck scan loops (`_ticket_dirs` iterations in src/rebar/_commands/fsck_scan.py) ... are O(all tickets ever created)'","Plan Approach step 2: 'Switch the fsck scan loops to it' (the active-only iterator)","fsck_scan.py _check_json_validity/_check_create_events call `_ticket_dirs(tracker, include_archived=True)` unconditionally because they sum a STORE-WIDE authorship tally; `include_archived` scopes only whether a dir's findings are REPORTED (via `_dir_is_archived`), not whether the dir is walked/reduced"],"finding":"The plan claims active-only scoping applies uniformly to 'the fsck scan loops', but the JSON-validity and create-events checks feed store-wide authorship tallies and must still walk every ticket dir; scoping there can only affect which findings are REPORTED, not which dirs are visited.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f6275098a48ca87d2","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 2 / Scope: src/rebar/_commands/fsck_scan.py","norm_id":"nd5ccd0c65018307f","priority":0.0587,"reason":"veto:cited-reference-inaccurate","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A store with many archived tickets: fsck's json-validity and create-events passes still read/reduce every archived dir, so the O(all tickets) walk cost the plan targets is not eliminated for those two checks","An implementer taking 'switch the scan loops to the active-only iterator' literally could scope the tally checks to active-only and silently drop archived tickets' signed/unsigned counts from the store-wide authorship line"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"In step 2 and the fsck_scan.py scope line, split the two behaviours: state that snapshot/forward-compat checks iterate the active-only iterator, but the authorship-tally checks (checks 1 and 2) always walk all dirs and apply `include_archived` to gate which dirs' findings are reported (matching the existing `_dir_is_archived` reporting guard).","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2222,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"no","cited_reference_accurate":"no","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"yes","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_ve